Source: create-network-tshoot-livecd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ciro Iriarte <ciro.iriarte+software@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/ciroiriarte/obs-network-tools

Package: create-network-tshoot-livecd
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, live-build, debootstrap, xorriso, curl, gpg, ca-certificates
Description: Build a boot-only network cabling-diagnostics LiveCD
 Builds a distro-independent live ISO (via live-build) that boots a target
 host into a RAM-resident diagnostic environment. On boot it identifies the
 host from a CSV persona inventory, brings up every physical NIC, runs
 nic-xray and lldpd, and prints a per-NIC cabling / LLDP-neighbour report to
 the VGA console and an auto-discovered serial console, then drops to a root
 shell. It writes nothing to local disks.
 .
 Requires a Debian or Ubuntu build host with live-build. On Ubuntu, install
 the live-build package from this same repository, as the distribution's
 stock live-build is too old to build a current image.
